<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
Thank you for your application to travel with your dog, [insert name of dog] in the aircraft cabin with Qantas.<br />
<br />
Qantas has reviewed all information provided and is currently unable to grant permission for your dog, [<strong>insert name of dog</strong>] to travel in the aircraft cabin. Qantas must be satisfied that it is safe to carry your dog in the aircraft cabin. &nbsp;If your situation changes, including if your dog meets the <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/travelling-with-specific-needs/service-dogs.html#criteria-for-carriage">Criteria for Carriage</a>&nbsp;in future, we would welcome an application from you at that time.<br />
<br />
As you are currently unable to travel with your dog in the aircraft cabin, we can explore alternatives with you, including the offer of a full refund for any flights you have booked but not yet undertaken. If you decide to proceed with your flight/s, your dog may still travel with Qantas, however carriage must be in the aircraft’s cargo hold in accordance with <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/travelling-with-pets.html">Qantas Freight requirements</a>.</body>
</html>